.TH GIT LOG VIM 1 glo\-@VERSION@
.SH NAME
glo \- git log on (neo)vim
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glo
.RB [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The program glo is a wrapper script to view git logs inside vim and neovim
without additional plugins

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "help, \-h, \-\-help"
Print brief usage information to standard output and exit.
.TP
.B "-v, \-\-version"
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B "-u"
View commits since last release tag.
.TP
.B "-n <NUM>"
View last NUM of commits.
.B "-c <tag/hash>...<tag/hash>"
View commits from tag/hash to tag/hash, this is just passed directly to git log.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.P
The configuration of glo is located at:
.B ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-${HOME}/.config}/gitlog-vim/configrc

.P
To see the location of the configuration file and generating it if running for
the first time, run glo with the help flag.

.P
The configuration defines the following options:

.TP
.B
vim_bin
The vim binary to execute, if you usually run vim through a wrapper this is the
place to specify it as the vim binary, so long as the wrapper is in your PATH
the full path is not needed.

.TP
.B
vim_type
The type of vim (vim or neovim) you use, for achieving the intended function
there is just one line of vimscript that differs between vim and neovim so this
is necessary for the script to work as intended.
accepted values are: vim, neovim

